  "designReference": "https://support.activision.com/call-of-duty--wwii/articles/call-of-duty-wwii-multiplayer",
  "note": "Custom LAN tuning based on retail CoD2. These overrides are not official WWII statistics. Preserve original cadence, magazines and reloads. Players have 105 health (browser_player_health.py). Damage follows the cartridge: up close a 7.62x25mm round deals 30 (four shots to the body), 9x19mm 35 and .45 ACP or .455 Webley 40 (three), the intermediate 7.92x33mm Kurz and .30 Carbine 42 (three), and a full-power rifle round 45 from an automatic weapon (three), 45 doubled to the chest from a semi-automatic rifle (two) and 90 from a bolt-action rifle (one). A pistol deals what a submachine gun firing its round deals and loses it sooner. Pistol rounds fall to 10: in SMGs firing 700 rounds a minute or more from 600 to 1,500 units, in slower ones from 700 to 2,000, with 0.5 degrees of aimed spread. In automatic rifles the intermediate round falls to 32 from 1,200 to 2,500 units and full-power rounds to their retail 40 from 1,500 to 2,500, with 0.2 degrees of aimed spread; semi-automatic and bolt-action rifles, the M1 Carbine included, keep theirs at every range. No automatic weapon kills with one headshot, and two do; bolt-action rifles kill with one shot to the body, semi-automatic rifles, the Colt and the Webley with one to the head up close, the Luger and TT-30 with two. Weapons that share a class, damage, rate of fire, zoom and bullet share one damage model.",
  "recoil": {
    "note": "Aimed recoil follows each gun's free recoil: impulse = bullet mass x muzzle velocity + charge mass x gas velocity, energy = impulse^2 / (2 x loaded mass), times the PPSh-41's compensator and the PPS-43's and SVT-40's muzzle brakes. One aimed shot moves the sights singleShot degrees per square root of a joule, camera and gun together; half a second of automatic fire climbs automaticClimb degrees per square root of a joule per round a second. Each gun keeps the shape of its retail kick: its sideways and hip kicks and its gun kick scale with it. Every automatic weapon recentres at 1,700, every semi-automatic rifle at 1,480 and every pistol at 1,400; the G43 takes the Garand's and SVT-40's aimed gun spring, and the M1 Carbine kicks to either side instead of always to the right.",
